  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "CUBESETCOUNT counts tuples in a held CUBESET (including 0 for [Measures].Members), propagates errors, and returns #N/A for non-cube values",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, CUBESETCOUNT(set) returns the tuple count of a CUBESET cell (returning 0 for an empty set such as [Measures].Members), propagates scalar errors (#VALUE!, #DIV/0!, #NUM!, #REF!, #NAME?), and returns #N/A for non-cube values such as blanks, numbers, or plain text (and #VALUE! for a cell holding a CUBEMEMBER). All 3,078 full-bank CUBESETCOUNT rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in DnaCalc crates/calc-host/tests/fixtures/cube/measured.xlsx (A58-A67, A130) and CalcFunc-Evidence admit2-answers-cubesetcount-special.json; 3,078/3,078 full-bank rows match.",
